  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "William Lawrence Stephenson was a British retailer who helped establish Woolworth's British business and later became its managing director and chairman. Recruited for his buying experience, he adapted the American variety-store model to British suppliers and shoppers. His leadership helped turn the company into one of the country's largest retail chains.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 93,
